  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-element permutation with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>j</mi></math>, such that either <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are consecutive integers or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are consecutive integers.&nbsp;Then the number of such permutations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
